{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":408752,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"aa988f28-5787-4ecb-b964-a3bffae978f9","total_cost_usd":1.3182809999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42576,"cache_read_input_tokens":20240,"output_tokens":34143,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":42576,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":34143,"cache_read_input_tokens":20240,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42576,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":42576},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":28711,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.028816,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":34143,"cacheReadInputTokens":20240,"cacheCreationInputTokens":42576,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.2894649999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"debris-designer\",\n  \"size_classes\": {\n    \"small\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 1,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 2,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": true\n    },\n    \"medium\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 2,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 4,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": true\n    },\n    \"oversized\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 6,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 12,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  \"debris\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"bent_truss_section\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Bent Truss Section\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 430,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"A folded aluminium lattice off a broken solar boom — the bread-and-butter haul of the low sky, cheap per kilo but it crushes flat and never argues on the way down.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"crumpled_foil_blanket\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Crumpled Foil Blanket\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 45,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 16,\n      \"notes\": \"A whole satellite's worth of shredded multi-layer insulation balled up and tumbling — the lightest thing in the sky by a factor of five, which makes it the piece a beginner learns the tether on.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"burnt_panel_offcut\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Burnt Panel Offcut\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 85,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 13,\n      \"notes\": \"A scorched honeycomb face sheet torn off a bus panel, already half-cooked by its own decaying orbit and worth taking only because it costs almost nothing to carry.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"spent_bolt_cluster\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Spent Bolt Cluster\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 130,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 15,\n      \"notes\": \"A knot of frangible separation bolts still welded to their collar — dense lumps of good steel that Armstrong will always take off your hands.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_antenna_whip\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Antenna Whip\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 35,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"A hairline-split monopole that glints on a slow cycle across the whole band — the cheapest possible lesson in what fragile costs you, since it weighs nothing and still can't be crushed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scorched_hull_plate\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Scorched Hull Plate\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 700,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 7,\n      \"notes\": \"A curved slab of pressure-vessel skin with its ring frames still attached, the heaviest thing down here that a hand magnet will hold — three and a half times the average piece, and the first load that makes the jetpack feel like it's pushing a train.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dented_pressure_bottle\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Dented Pressure Bottle\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 380,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A spent cold-gas tank, vented and safe, packing more mass into one crushed slot than anything else in the band — the best mass-to-slot bargain the low sky offers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"shattered_lens_cowl\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Shattered Lens Cowl\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 70,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"The glass sunshade off a cheap earth-imager, spidered but intact, orbiting well clear of the common clumps so reaching it is a deliberate crossing rather than a drift.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"collapsed_launch_shroud\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Collapsed Launch Shroud\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1100,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"Half a payload fairing, folded like a dropped umbrella — mostly enclosed air, so it is bulk rather than tonnage, and crane-cable only regardless. It sits in the sky all semester as a visible advertisement for an upgrade the shipping slice does not sell.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"reaction_wheel_housing\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Reaction Wheel Housing\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 870,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A cast steel gimbal block with the flywheel still seized inside — the workhorse of the low band, solid enough to shrug off a mediocre landing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"severed_solar_wing_spar\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Severed Solar Wing Spar\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 760,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"The load-bearing backbone of an array with the cells sheared away, long enough that it swings wide on every turn and teaches the player to stop before slewing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_solar_array\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Solar Array\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 390,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"A wing panel of intact gallium cells behind fractured cover glass — the signature fragile piece of the slice, four uncrushed slots forever and double damage from every mistake.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"battery_pack_module\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Battery Pack Module\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1150,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"A brick of lithium cells in a machined frame — the heaviest hand-tetherable piece in the shipping slice, and the one that decides whether a two-tether string is a good idea.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"thruster_nozzle_bell\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Thruster Nozzle Bell\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 340,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 11,\n      \"notes\": \"A niobium bell off an attitude thruster, dense and compact, the piece that makes a one-slot capture feel worth the crossing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"star_tracker_head\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Star Tracker Head\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 155,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"A baffled optical head the size of a beer keg, light for the band and precious and utterly uncrushable — the cheapest way to learn that fragile is about bulk and risk, not weight.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tangled_harness_bundle\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Tangled Harness Bundle\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 210,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 12,\n      \"notes\": \"A snarl of copper loom torn out of a bus, floppy on the cable and forgiving of every rough latch — the low band's filler, and its safety net on a thin run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"parabolic_dish_section\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Parabolic Dish Section\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 420,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"A quarter-segment of a mesh reflector on its own faster orbit, catching the light on a slow cycle — a real ship manoeuvre to reach and a patient closing rate to latch.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"derelict_upper_stage_tank\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Derelict Upper Stage Tank\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 2000,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A drained kick-stage tank the length of the rocket itself — thin-walled and hollow, so it is twelve uncrushed slots of nothing much, and crane-cable only. The piece the player circles once, measures with their eyes, and files away for later.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"comsat_bus_frame\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Comsat Bus Frame\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1950,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"The machined spine of a dead communications satellite, dense with fittings — the common piece of the top band and heavier on its own than most complete low-band hauls.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"hardened_avionics_core\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Hardened Avionics Core\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1600,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"A radiation-shielded flight computer in a lead-lined box, built to survive anything the sky could do to it — which is exactly why it survives the ride down too.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cryo_propellant_sphere\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cryo Propellant Sphere\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 2200,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"A thick-walled titanium sphere off a station-keeping system, the single heaviest thing a hand magnet will hold at any tier — one of these turns a routine reentry into a three-pass problem.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"momentum_gyro_cluster\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Momentum Gyro Cluster\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1150,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"Three control-moment gyros still bolted to their pedestal, absurdly dense for one crushed slot — the piece that proves mass, not volume, is what fills the top band's holds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sensor_boom_mast\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Sensor Boom Mast\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 700,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"A telescoping magnetometer boom, collapsed and locked — awkward to latch square, but it crushes into a single slot and asks nothing else of the flight home.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gallium_solar_panel\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Gallium Solar Panel\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 920,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"A full triple-junction wing off a high-orbit bird, worth several solid pieces of its own size class and worth nothing at all if the touchdown runs past five metres a second.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"optical_telescope_barrel\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Optical Telescope Barrel\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1300,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"A mirrored assembly in a carbon tube, heavy and fragile at once — four uncrushed slots, double heat damage, and the best payday in the catalog short of the satellite itself.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"xenon_ion_grid\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Xenon Ion Grid\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 540,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A stack of etched molybdenum accelerator grids in their mounting cage, spawning far off the clumps at real relative velocity — the purest latch-jerk test in the game.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"high_gain_dish_assembly\",\n      \"display_name\": \"High-Gain Dish Assembly\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 3200,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A full reflector with its feed tower and gimbal still attached — crane-cable only, and the rehearsal piece for the satellite: same technique, same order of mass, forgiving cargo.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"armstrongs_satellite\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Armstrong's Satellite\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 4200,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"The one he lost the day of the cascade, hanging above the top band — the heaviest object in the game, fragile and oversized, uncrushable at any tier, roughly doubling a fully upgraded ship on its own, and the win condition only if it comes down gently.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"band_summary\": [\n    {\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"piece_count\": 9,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.1,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 330.6\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"piece_count\": 9,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.2,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 699.4\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"piece_count\": 10,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.25,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 1776.0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"revision_notes\": [\n    \"Finding 1 accepted, and the lift is larger than the 10x asked for, for a reason worth stating. The Economy Balancer's 16.1 kg per slot is the spawn-weighted figure pooled across the whole shipping slice, but GDD 2.3.5's doubling is specified 'at starting storage size' — a beginner with a six-slot hold and a tier-1 compactor, flying suborbital. Suborbital alone sat at 10.8 kg/slot crushed and 8.2 kg/slot under a strict tier-1 compactor, well below the slice pool, so a 10x lift would have left the binding case at a 490-650 kg hold. Suborbital masses are raised ~14x and the rest of the catalog with them.\",\n    \"Finding 1, the resulting anchor, stated so the Economy Balancer does not have to re-derive it. Suborbital hand-tetherable junk now runs 214.5 kg per spawn-weighted cargo slot crushed and 124.9 kg under a strict tier-1 compactor, so a six-slot hold weighs 749 kg at tier 1 and 984 kg fully crushed. That puts dry_mass_kg at 750-985 rather than 90. Against the Researcher's shield Cd 1.5 and 3.1 m2 reference area, the staged empty ship lands at beta 161-212 kg/m2 and the staged full-hold ship at 322-423 kg/m2 — the full-hold case sits inside the 300-500 real-capsule band the Researcher cites, which is the configuration that actually flies the reentry.\",\n    \"Finding 2 accepted, but not through size_class. Both pieces named are already medium and GDD 2.3.4 fixes medium's slot cost at 2 crushed / 4 uncrushed, which the charter forbids me to tune, so the only lever I own is mass. scorched_hull_plate is now 700 kg against a spawn-weighted suborbital mean of 214.5 kg — 3.3x the average piece, up from 2.3x — and bent_truss_section is 430 kg at 2.0x. The band's mass spread is now 45 kg to 700 kg, a 15.6x range where it was 11.7x, so the tow mechanic has a genuine light end and a genuine heavy end to teach with before the player ever reaches the low band.\",\n    \"Finding 2, the one number I do not own and that has to move with this. The Balancer's '31% drop in EVA acceleration' implies a suit-plus-jetpack mass near 90 kg. At that suit mass the new hull plate would leave 11% of clean acceleration and a two-piece string 7%, which is not a train, it is a wall. A suited astronaut with an MMU-class pack is realistically 200-260 kg; at 250 kg one plate leaves 26% and two leave 15%, which is the handling the GDD describes. Suit mass is a config parameter, not a catalog field, so I am flagging it rather than fixing it.\",\n    \"The three crane-only pieces and the satellite are re-anchored rather than rescaled, and this is the one place I overrode the finding's arithmetic. GDD 2.3.7 asserts two things about Armstrong's satellite that only hold together at one scale: it is the heaviest object in the game, and it roughly doubles the ship's mass on its own. The old catalog satisfied neither honestly — 1,600 kg against an implied 90 kg ship was 18x, not 2x. Scaling it 14x with everything else would have made it 22,400 kg against a 900 kg ship. Instead the satellite is set to 4,200 kg, roughly twice a fully upgraded ship, and high_gain_dish_assembly (3,200), derelict_upper_stage_tank (2,000) and collapsed_launch_shroud (1,100) are placed underneath it in band order. This also makes them physically honest for the first time: fairings, drained stages and dish reflectors are bulk, not tonnage, which is exactly why they are oversized — the class is about what tool takes them and how many slots they eat, never about mass.\",\n    \"Nothing else changed. Every id, band, size_class, fragile flag and spawn_weight is byte-identical to the previous catalog; only mass_kg moved, plus four piece notes whose text made a mass claim that the new numbers would have falsified (crumpled_foil_blanket, scorched_hull_plate, dented_pressure_bottle, star_tracker_head, and the three oversized pieces' bulk-not-tonnage framing). The relative ordering the Economy Balancer priced against is untouched.\"\n  ],\n  \"design_notes\": [\n    \"Mass carries the difficulty curve, because the Researcher says heat cannot, and the band ratios that do that work survived the rescale intact. Entry speeds from the three bands differ by only 1,316 / 1,366 / 1,441 m/s, a v^3 heat spread of just 1.31x. Hand-tetherable mean mass is now 234.4 kg suborbital, 536.9 kg low, 1,295.0 kg high — steps of 2.29x and 2.41x, 5.5x end to end, against the previous catalog's 2.47x / 2.53x / 6.25x. Per cargo slot, spawn-weighted and crushed, the bands run 214.5 / 291.1 / 669.0 kg. A full hold of high-band junk raises ballistic coefficient roughly three times as hard as a full hold of foil blankets, which is the lever the Researcher explicitly points the crew at.\",\n    \"The full-hold doubling in GDD 2.3.5 is now a true statement rather than an aspiration, and it is true at the case that matters. A beginner with six slots and a tier-1 compactor filling up on suborbital junk comes home carrying 749 kg; crushed optimally the same hold is 984 kg. Either figure is the same order as the ship it is riding in, so the sluggish-full-hold feel the GDD promises arrives on the player's first successful run rather than at some upgrade tier.\",\n    \"Fragile fraction is spawn-weighted, not counted, and lands at exactly 0.10 / 0.20 / 0.25. The piece counts tell a different story on purpose: suborbital has 2 fragile types out of 9 (0.22 by count) but they carry weights 5 and 3 against a band total of 80, so the player meets one about one time in ten. The high band has 4 fragile types out of 10 (0.40 by count) weighted 6+5+2+1 against 56, giving 0.25. Counting types would have overstated the low sky and understated nothing.\",\n    \"Every size class and the fragile flag appear in the shipping slice. Suborbital and low each carry small, medium, fragile-small and fragile-medium, so a player who never buys past the hand magnet still meets the whole property space. The two crane-only pieces below the high band exist to be looked at and not taken — visible advertisements for the deferred crane magnet rather than dead entries.\",\n    \"Medium is distributed 2 / 5 / 5 across the bands rather than piled into the top. That keeps the GDD's 'higher bands skew toward medium' true as a proportion — 22% / 56% / 50% of types — without making the low band a small-only tutorial. The slot-cost pressure the high band is supposed to apply arrives through fragility and mass, not through medium count alone.\",\n    \"No piece is strictly best, and the rescale kept that true by preserving every ratio. The dense small pieces (dented pressure bottle at 380 kg in one crushed slot, momentum gyro cluster at 1,150) buy mass efficiency per slot at the cost of a heavier ride home; the light bulky ones (crumpled foil blanket, tangled harness bundle) are nearly free to tow and nearly worthless per trip; fragile pieces pay a premium the Economy Balancer sets but forfeit crushing forever and double every damage source. The greed decision is between axes, never along one.\",\n    \"The suborbital band now teaches the tow mechanic by itself. Its pieces run 45 kg to 700 kg — a 15.6x spread inside the first band the player ever flies — so the beat in GDD 2.3.4 where the jetpack starts feeling like it is pushing a train has a piece to land on before the low band opens. The heaviest hand-tetherable piece per band (700 / 1,150 / 2,200 kg) is also the specific case the Playtester should sweep hold force and shear against at each magnet tier.\",\n    \"The oversized class is bulk, not tonnage, and the masses now say so. A folded fairing half at 1,100 kg, a drained kick stage at 2,000 and a dish assembly at 3,200 each cost six crushed slots or twelve uncrushed — more hold than a starting ship has — while weighing between one and four times the heaviest piece a hand magnet will hold. That separation is deliberate: oversized is a statement about which tool takes the piece and how much hold it eats, and if it were also a statement about mass then Armstrong's satellite could not be both the heaviest object in the game and roughly double the ship, which GDD 2.3.7 requires of it simultaneously.\",\n    \"Armstrong's satellite is authored into the high band at 4,200 kg because the GDD places it above the top band and there is no fourth band name to use. It is fragile and oversized — the worst combination — with spawn weight 1, so it contributes 0.018 of the high band's spawn weight and does not distort the fragile gradient. Treat its band field as a bookkeeping placement, not a spawn location; it is a fixed object, not a member of the loot table.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":323519,"ttft_stream_ms":1470,"time_to_request_ms":221,"type":"result","duration_ms":405572,"uuid":"af0d2e34-4d1d-4173-916f-e70b05d53f99"}
